{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3j4fe17XaG15s9h4kEF","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed or committed anything. A per-day breakdown in `out/summary.csv` would break the portal pull.\n\n**Why:** the docstring in `scripts/summarize.py` says the file must stay `period,total,count`, one row per period, under 50 lines, because the portal rejects extra columns and silently cuts off anything past 50 lines. The 2025 data covers 248 distinct days. Day rows would push the file to about 260 lines. The portal would keep only the first ~50 rows, and since the \"silently\" part means it doesn't flag the cut, the partner would get incomplete numbers without knowing. Adding a day column instead would get the whole file rejected.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **A separate file**, e.g. `out/summary_daily.csv`. I'd recommend this. `summary.csv` stays as it is, and the partner gets the day rows another way. Can the portal pull a second file?\n2. **Find out whether the portal's 50-line limit can be raised.** If it can, the day rows could go into `summary.csv`.\n3. **Something shorter that fits under 50 lines**, e.g. per-week (about 52 rows, so slightly too many) or only some months by day.\n\nWhich one should I do? Or is there a different route to the partner?","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":409,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":20411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":199,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-42>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T23:57:13.524Z","request_id":"gen-1794700628-8hl2b19Y02FRBKykP1G5"}
